+ * Describes how far a date is from now in words: "3 minutes ago", "in 2 days", "just now". The time between the
+ * two is rounded down to whole units, so 3 minutes 59 seconds is "3 minutes", and the unit is the largest that fits:
+ *   under 10 seconds   "just now" (also for the future)    1 to 6 days      "N days"
+ *   10 to 59 seconds   "N seconds"                         7 to 29 days     "N weeks" (1 to 4)
+ *   1 to 59 minutes    "N minutes"                         30 to 364 days   "N months" (1 to 11, of 30 days)
+ *   1 to 23 hours      "N hours"                           365 days or more "N years" (of 365 days)
+ * followed by " ago" for a date in the past, and preceded by "in " for one in the future. One is singular
