+ * since there is nothing to average. The sum is compensated for rounding error, so ten 0.1s average to
+ * exactly 0.1 (a plain running total gives 0.09999999999999999), and it does not overflow when the numbers
+ * are finite, so mean([Number.MAX_VALUE, Number.MAX_VALUE]) is Number.MAX_VALUE. NaN and infinities follow
+ * normal arithmetic: any NaN gives NaN,
+ * Infinity and -Infinity together give NaN, and Infinity alone gives Infinity. xs is not changed.
