+ * (2.5, NaN, Infinity) are false. It is fast for every safe integer, using trial division by small primes and
+ * then the Miller-Rabin test with the first twelve primes as bases, which is exact below 3.3e24. Integers
+ * above Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER are not stored exactly, so whether they are prime has no meaning and they throw.
