+/**
+ * Converts a Roman numeral to a number, the inverse of toRoman: fromRoman("MCMXCIV") is 1994. Only the
+ * numerals toRoman can produce are accepted, so the result is always from 1 to 3999 and
+ * toRoman(fromRoman(s)) gives back s. Anything else is rejected, not guessed at: the empty string, other
+ * ways of writing a number ("IIII", "VX", "IC", "MMMM"), letters outside I V X L C D M, and spaces. The
+ * letters may be all upper case or all lower case ("mcmxciv"), but not mixed.
+ * @param {string} roman
