+
+/**
+ * Counts the words in a string. A word is a run of letters, digits or combining marks (in any
+ * script); whitespace and punctuation separate words, so "well-known" is two words. An apostrophe
+ * between two letters stays inside the word, so "don't" is one.
+ * @param {string} s
+ * @returns {number} The number of words; 0 for an empty string or one with no letters or digits.
+ * @throws {TypeError} If s is not a string.
+ */
