+ * Returns the uppercased first letter of each word in a name, e.g. "Ada King Lovelace" gives "AKL".
+ * Words are found as in countWords, so whitespace and punctuation separate them: "Jean-Luc Picard"
+ * gives "JLP", while "O'Brien" is one word and gives "O". A letter keeps its accent even when the
+ * accent is a separate combining mark.
