+/**
+ * Reverses the order of the words in a sentence, e.g. "the quick brown fox" gives "fox brown quick the".
+ * Words are separated by whitespace only, so punctuation stays attached to its word
+ * ("Hello, world!" gives "world! Hello,"). Runs of whitespace, including tabs and newlines, become a
+ * single space, and leading and trailing whitespace is dropped.
